{"id": "c3881419-eaf5-42fa-86fc-27f49d1f1c2d", "name": "IdeaM -- Competitive Intelligence", "rootNodeId": "root-compintel", "nodes": {"root-compintel": {"id": "root-compintel", "name": "IdeaM -- Competitive Intelligence", "content": "<p><strong>Living competitive-intelligence log.</strong> Each week a market brief (currently the ChatGPT-5 weekly AI report) is captured here, analyzed for impact on IdeaM's position, and its recommendations rolled up into a single tracked priority list.</p><p>Read the <strong>Rolling Priorities</strong> section to see where we stand at a glance; read <strong>Weekly Briefs</strong> for the source material and our analysis of each week.</p><p>Guiding thesis (from Brief 001): the market is converging on <strong>AI that acts on structured information while the user stays in control</strong> — structural, inspectable, reversible. That is already our stated identity; our hierarchical outline gives us a head start. Win it first and loudly.</p>", "type": "chapter", "parentId": null, "childrenIds": ["e4fd791b-0cea-491c-9ba7-f631f955bce4", "7601f947-9860-4ee8-a9bc-ca1f2d03020f", "854393b2-e726-4ccf-b48b-3bf1b831cd1e"], "isCollapsed": false, "prefix": "", "metadata": {"userEdited": true}}, "e4fd791b-0cea-491c-9ba7-f631f955bce4": {"id": "e4fd791b-0cea-491c-9ba7-f631f955bce4", "name": "How this works — legend & cadence", "content": "", "type": "chapter", "parentId": "root-compintel", "childrenIds": ["e3fcbab5-229b-4c16-8fa0-a59f30759bdd", "76bd38b6-9398-4a9a-8bf8-d8d24c034476", "18435a8b-abb5-4b56-ba7b-7ba4729aa5ca"], "isCollapsed": false, "prefix": "1", "metadata": {"userEdited": true}}, "e3fcbab5-229b-4c16-8fa0-a59f30759bdd": {"id": "e3fcbab5-229b-4c16-8fa0-a59f30759bdd", "name": "Cadence", "content": "<p>A new brief lands roughly weekly. Each becomes a dated section under <strong>Weekly Briefs</strong>, holding the source report and our analysis. Recurring recommendations roll up (deduped) into <strong>Rolling Priorities</strong> so we can see what keeps surfacing and what we've shipped against it.</p>", "type": "document", "parentId": "e4fd791b-0cea-491c-9ba7-f631f955bce4", "childrenIds": [], "isCollapsed": false, "prefix": "1.1", "metadata": {"createdAt": 1788552182282, "updatedAt": 1788552182282}}, "76bd38b6-9398-4a9a-8bf8-d8d24c034476": {"id": "76bd38b6-9398-4a9a-8bf8-d8d24c034476", "name": "Signal labels", "content": "<ul><li><strong>ACT NOW</strong> — build/decide this cycle; competitors are shipping it.</li><li><strong>ACT SOON</strong> — next in queue, sequence after the current flagship.</li><li><strong>INVESTIGATE</strong> — prototype/validate before committing.</li><li><strong>MONITOR</strong> — watch; no action yet.</li></ul>", "type": "document", "parentId": "e4fd791b-0cea-491c-9ba7-f631f955bce4", "childrenIds": [], "isCollapsed": false, "prefix": "1.2", "metadata": {"createdAt": 1788552182282, "updatedAt": 1788552182282}}, "18435a8b-abb5-4b56-ba7b-7ba4729aa5ca": {"id": "18435a8b-abb5-4b56-ba7b-7ba4729aa5ca", "name": "Priority status", "content": "<ul><li><strong>Not started</strong></li><li><strong>Investigating</strong></li><li><strong>Building</strong></li><li><strong>Shipped</strong></li></ul>", "type": "document", "parentId": "e4fd791b-0cea-491c-9ba7-f631f955bce4", "childrenIds": [], "isCollapsed": false, "prefix": "1.3", "metadata": {"createdAt": 1788552182282, "updatedAt": 1788552182282}}, "7601f947-9860-4ee8-a9bc-ca1f2d03020f": {"id": "7601f947-9860-4ee8-a9bc-ca1f2d03020f", "name": "🟠 Rolling Priorities (living roll-up)", "content": "<p>The deduped, tracked priority list across all briefs. This is the page to check. Seeded from Brief 001 (Aug 28–Sep 4, 2026).</p>", "type": "chapter", "parentId": "root-compintel", "childrenIds": ["f70c7286-962c-4dc8-a02d-cd1e5445e02c", "24f93245-b149-4f12-96dc-5f30ce8f4f78", "c4c7f45e-e89a-43f4-8043-f81ff896f62e", "0cfa6f60-f61b-4dc5-8758-743429b49b13", "82e5da78-b97a-4a7f-8f20-e64884ceac99", "518ab30b-74c6-4b2e-a029-eb593f157e28", "969b676a-8aff-46ff-9ecc-240975758ed7"], "isCollapsed": false, "prefix": "2", "metadata": {"userEdited": true}}, "f70c7286-962c-4dc8-a02d-cd1e5445e02c": {"id": "f70c7286-962c-4dc8-a02d-cd1e5445e02c", "name": "P1 · Proposed Changes mode  —  ACT NOW  ·  status: ~HALF-BUILT (extend existing engine)", "content": "<p><strong>The flagship.</strong> Every AI operation that changes the outline shows its changes for approval BEFORE they become permanent: additions provisional, deletions struck-through-but-kept, moves showing the old parent, rewrites as before/after — with approve / reject / approve-all.</p><p><strong>Why it's ours to win:</strong> a direct extension of our codified values (user-in-control, outline-data-protection-paramount, derivative-by-default), and our hierarchy makes it MORE natural than a doc tool. Notion/Capacities are adding this on top of doc/database models; we already think this way.</p><p>🟠 <strong>Audit finding — we're already ~half there</strong> and we have a GOLD-STANDARD reference already shipped (Refresh-from-Web / LIVE BOOKS: mandatory per-node before/after diff, per-node checkboxes, approve-all, nothing applies until confirmed). See 2.1.1.</p><p><strong>Next slice (highest value):</strong> wrap the two most DANGEROUS lightweight ops — the natural-language Tell-AI delete and AI sub-outline insertion — in the same approve-gate, then unify all ops under one consistent 'provisional overlay' reusing the existing preview types and node-row styling.</p><p><strong>Absorbs</strong> Brief 001 #1 (pending op shown as a temporary node, not a hidden chat).</p>", "type": "document", "parentId": "7601f947-9860-4ee8-a9bc-ca1f2d03020f", "childrenIds": [], "isCollapsed": false, "prefix": "2.1", "metadata": {"userEdited": true}}, "24f93245-b149-4f12-96dc-5f30ce8f4f78": {"id": "24f93245-b149-4f12-96dc-5f30ce8f4f78", "name": "↳ Where we stand today (audit, Sep 2026)", "content": "<p><strong>Verdict: very feasible — unification & extension, not from scratch.</strong> The preview/approve engine, snapshots, undo, and node-styling hooks all already exist.</p><p><strong>Operations that ALREADY preview + approve (and default to a derivative, not overwrite):</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Transform outline</strong> — before/after + change counts; saves a new outline by default.</li><li><strong>Reformat content</strong> — side-by-side before/after; derivative by default.</li><li><strong>Summarize outline</strong> — preview; writes a new outline by default.</li><li><strong>Translate</strong> — per-node accept/reject via the shared transform engine.</li><li>🟠 <strong>Refresh-from-Web (LIVE BOOKS)</strong> — the GOLD STANDARD: mandatory per-node before/after diff, individual checkboxes + approve-all, nothing applies until you confirm. This IS the Proposed Changes pattern, already built.</li></ul><p><strong>Operations that still APPLY-DIRECTLY (undo-backed, but no approval preview) — the gap:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Expand / Generate content</strong> — applies into the editor; only a placement chooser (replace/append/prepend).</li><li><strong>Generate sub-outline</strong> — inserts children straight in.</li><li><strong>Tell-AI natural-language command</strong> — confirms intent in words ('shall I do X?') but doesn't show the RESULT for approval; deletes apply directly.</li></ul><p><strong>Reusable infrastructure (strong):</strong></p><ul><li>Unlimited-depth undo/redo with labeled actions.</li><li>Automatic timestamped snapshots before any transform (20 kept/outline) + Backup/Restore dialog + 'unmerge' backup.</li><li>A derivative-outline builder.</li><li>Node data model with a metadata object (already carries transform provenance; before/after fields exist in the proposal type).</li><li>Node-row styling hooks already in place: yellow highlight, multi-select ring, line-through, amber badges — the visual vocabulary for a provisional overlay.</li></ul><p><strong>Smallest valuable first slice:</strong> effectively already shipped for Transform/Refresh — so the next slice is wrapping AI sub-outline insertion and the NL add/delete in the same approve gate.</p><p><strong>Most dangerous today (fix first):</strong> the Tell-AI <em>delete</em> (deletes on intent-confirmation, no result preview) and AI sub-outline insertion.</p>", "type": "document", "parentId": "7601f947-9860-4ee8-a9bc-ca1f2d03020f", "childrenIds": [], "isCollapsed": false, "prefix": "2.1.1", "metadata": {"createdAt": 1788552265942, "updatedAt": 1788552265942}}, "c4c7f45e-e89a-43f4-8043-f81ff896f62e": {"id": "c4c7f45e-e89a-43f4-8043-f81ff896f62e", "name": "P2 · AI cost model: light / medium / heavy + pre-op approval  —  ACT NOW  ·  status: Ahead, needs formalizing", "content": "<p>Model three usage classes — light (organize/classify), medium (document generation), heavy (research, audio, video, podcast) — and require explicit approval before an expensive operation.</p><p><strong>Where we stand:</strong> we're ahead of the market — no company key, BYOK, priced-to-margin, metered, three-door allowance prompt, cost guardrails. Brief 001 #5's warning against 'unlimited AI' is nearly our own rule.</p><p><strong>The sharpening:</strong> the new heavy media features (Veo video, Lyria music — see the Google brainstorm) must be built ON TOP OF explicit pre-op approval, not bolted on. Capacities dropped BYOK and pushed external AI to MCP — we already have an MCP server, so that rail is started.</p>", "type": "document", "parentId": "7601f947-9860-4ee8-a9bc-ca1f2d03020f", "childrenIds": [], "isCollapsed": false, "prefix": "2.2", "metadata": {"createdAt": 1788552182282, "updatedAt": 1788552182282}}, "0cfa6f60-f61b-4dc5-8758-743429b49b13": {"id": "0cfa6f60-f61b-4dc5-8758-743429b49b13", "name": "P3 · Natural-language dynamic outline branches  —  ACT SOON  ·  status: Not started", "content": "<p>Turn a request into VISIBLE, editable criteria the user can correct, and save the result as a live outline branch / named view (not a disappearing chat answer).</p><p><strong>Align to:</strong> Howard's 1988 search-shaper spec — extend that, don't reinvent it. Same inspectable pattern as the flagship.</p>", "type": "document", "parentId": "7601f947-9860-4ee8-a9bc-ca1f2d03020f", "childrenIds": [], "isCollapsed": false, "prefix": "2.3", "metadata": {"createdAt": 1788552182282, "updatedAt": 1788552182282}}, "82e5da78-b97a-4a7f-8f20-e64884ceac99": {"id": "82e5da78-b97a-4a7f-8f20-e64884ceac99", "name": "P4 · Board / Kanban view from a subtree  —  INVESTIGATE  ·  status: Not started", "content": "<p>One outline, another representation: parent → board, children → columns, grandchildren → cards; moving a card changes the hierarchy. Outline stays the single source of truth — do NOT build a second database model or clone Notion.</p><p><strong>Where we stand:</strong> we already generate mind-maps and flowcharts from a subtree, so 'multiple views of one outline' is established; a board is the natural next view.</p>", "type": "document", "parentId": "7601f947-9860-4ee8-a9bc-ca1f2d03020f", "childrenIds": [], "isCollapsed": false, "prefix": "2.4", "metadata": {"createdAt": 1788552182282, "updatedAt": 1788552182282}}, "518ab30b-74c6-4b2e-a029-eb593f157e28": {"id": "518ab30b-74c6-4b2e-a029-eb593f157e28", "name": "P5 · Apple App Intents / Siri entry point  —  INVESTIGATE  ·  status: Not started", "content": "<p>Let users say 'add this to IdeaM', 'find my outline about X', 'summarize the unresolved decisions', 'continue the outline on screen' — Siri as a distribution entry point, with entities exposed to Siri but WITHOUT unrestricted edit authority.</p><p>🟠 <strong>The sleeper:</strong> Apple's note that qualifying small developers get some Private Cloud Compute model access WITHOUT API charges = a potential company-cost-free premium-AI path, which fits our no-company-key rule perfectly. Worth serious attention.</p><p><strong>Catch:</strong> we're Capacitor-based, so App Intents needs real native Swift work — medium-term. Target before iOS 27 maturity.</p>", "type": "document", "parentId": "7601f947-9860-4ee8-a9bc-ca1f2d03020f", "childrenIds": [], "isCollapsed": false, "prefix": "2.5", "metadata": {"createdAt": 1788552182282, "updatedAt": 1788552182282}}, "969b676a-8aff-46ff-9ecc-240975758ed7": {"id": "969b676a-8aff-46ff-9ecc-240975758ed7", "name": "P6 · Voice acts while you keep talking  —  INVESTIGATE (mostly absorbed into P1)  ·  status: Watch", "content": "<p>Tana's voice agent runs background requests during a meeting without interrupting. Compelling, but 🟠 note the tension: we DELIBERATELY pulled voice back from command-and-control to dictation-only (never auto-execute a misheard command). We would not reverse that. The valuable half — showing the pending op as a temporary node — is already covered by P1.</p>", "type": "document", "parentId": "7601f947-9860-4ee8-a9bc-ca1f2d03020f", "childrenIds": [], "isCollapsed": false, "prefix": "2.6", "metadata": {"createdAt": 1788552182282, "updatedAt": 1788552182282}}, "854393b2-e726-4ccf-b48b-3bf1b831cd1e": {"id": "854393b2-e726-4ccf-b48b-3bf1b831cd1e", "name": "Weekly Briefs", "content": "", "type": "chapter", "parentId": "root-compintel", "childrenIds": ["250f1cc9-166f-4d4f-88cc-df29b63ac518"], "isCollapsed": false, "prefix": "3", "metadata": {"userEdited": true}}, "250f1cc9-166f-4d4f-88cc-df29b63ac518": {"id": "250f1cc9-166f-4d4f-88cc-df29b63ac518", "name": "Brief 001 · Aug 28 – Sep 4, 2026", "content": "<p><strong>Source:</strong> ChatGPT-5 weekly 'Product Intelligence Brief' commissioned by Howard to track AI changes affecting our competitive position. Treat seriously.</p><p><strong>Overall signal:</strong> PKM competitors are moving beyond 'AI chat attached to notes.' The emerging model is AI that acts on structured information while keeping the user in control.</p>", "type": "chapter", "parentId": "854393b2-e726-4ccf-b48b-3bf1b831cd1e", "childrenIds": ["801c70b2-ce86-4e97-a6a3-9022a167f32f", "369363d6-e585-4987-913e-127c24da35c3", "aeed8cfe-36b5-4511-8936-bd2c4204e5a2", "a6c8e4ba-21a0-4dc3-8288-25e68a596303", "cbfb85e3-3854-4a33-8182-243d25b063cf", "f819d744-f142-4826-83c9-7e834d6df54a", "42090047-3c0b-4146-a3e8-7728fe17fc30", "1e8b808d-90ee-4b54-a1f1-1d4833292bd3"], "isCollapsed": false, "prefix": "3.1", "metadata": {"userEdited": true}}, "801c70b2-ce86-4e97-a6a3-9022a167f32f": {"id": "801c70b2-ce86-4e97-a6a3-9022a167f32f", "name": "① Tana — multitasking voice agent", "content": "<p><strong>What changed:</strong> Tana's voice agent executes several background requests during a meeting (research, find notes, update docs, operate connected tools) without interrupting; added customizable daily-brief agents and natural-language search.</p><p><strong>Why it matters:</strong> combines voice capture + context awareness + parallel agent execution + structured storage — no stopping to open an AI window and re-explain context.</p><p><strong>Report rec:</strong> INVESTIGATE — prototype one background outline operation that runs while the user keeps dictating; show the pending op as a temporary child node, not a hidden chat.</p>", "type": "document", "parentId": "250f1cc9-166f-4d4f-88cc-df29b63ac518", "childrenIds": [], "isCollapsed": false, "prefix": "3.1.1", "metadata": {"createdAt": 1788552182282, "updatedAt": 1788552182282}}, "369363d6-e585-4987-913e-127c24da35c3": {"id": "369363d6-e585-4987-913e-127c24da35c3", "name": "② AI becoming inspectable rather than invisible", "content": "<p><strong>What changed:</strong> Notion agents propose line-level edits users approve individually; Capacities previews proposed object/property changes before approve/deny.</p><p><strong>Why it matters:</strong> the pattern is AI proposes → affected content identified → user approves/rejects → only approved changes persist. Reduces fear of quiet damage.</p><p><strong>Report rec:</strong> ACT NOW — a unified Proposed Changes mode (provisional adds, struck-through deletes, moves showing old parent, rewrite comparison, approve/reject/approve-all). A meaningful trust advantage.</p>", "type": "document", "parentId": "250f1cc9-166f-4d4f-88cc-df29b63ac518", "childrenIds": [], "isCollapsed": false, "prefix": "3.1.2", "metadata": {"createdAt": 1788552182282, "updatedAt": 1788552182282}}, "aeed8cfe-36b5-4511-8936-bd2c4204e5a2": {"id": "aeed8cfe-36b5-4511-8936-bd2c4204e5a2", "name": "③ Natural-language search produces visible structure", "content": "<p><strong>What changed:</strong> Tana converts 'meetings with Sarah last week' into editable filter controls the user can inspect and adjust.</p><p><strong>Why it matters:</strong> a generated query becomes a reusable working object instead of a disappearing answer.</p><p><strong>Report rec:</strong> ACT NOW — expose the generated criteria; let users save the result as a dynamic branch or named view.</p>", "type": "document", "parentId": "250f1cc9-166f-4d4f-88cc-df29b63ac518", "childrenIds": [], "isCollapsed": false, "prefix": "3.1.3", "metadata": {"createdAt": 1788552182282, "updatedAt": 1788552182282}}, "a6c8e4ba-21a0-4dc3-8288-25e68a596303": {"id": "a6c8e4ba-21a0-4dc3-8288-25e68a596303", "name": "④ Outliners absorbing database & board behavior", "content": "<p><strong>What changed:</strong> Obsidian 1.14 adds a Kanban layout to Bases (grouping, drag-reorder, collapsible groups) and fixes large-vault performance; Workflowy expanding into tables, calendars, timelines, boards, multiple panes.</p><p><strong>Why it matters:</strong> users expect one body of information in several representations (outline, table, board, calendar, presentation).</p><p><strong>Report rec:</strong> INVESTIGATE — a lightweight board view (parent → board, children → columns, grandchildren → cards; moving a card changes hierarchy). Keep the outline as source of truth; don't build a second database model.</p>", "type": "document", "parentId": "250f1cc9-166f-4d4f-88cc-df29b63ac518", "childrenIds": [], "isCollapsed": false, "prefix": "3.1.4", "metadata": {"createdAt": 1788552182282, "updatedAt": 1788552182282}}, "cbfb85e3-3854-4a33-8182-243d25b063cf": {"id": "cbfb85e3-3854-4a33-8182-243d25b063cf", "name": "⑤ Competitors exposing the real cost of embedded AI", "content": "<p><strong>What changed:</strong> Capacities added larger monthly AI budgets, paid top-ups, auto top-ups, and REMOVED bring-your-own-key (arguing media/orchestration can't run reliably on arbitrary keys); external AI now via MCP.</p><p><strong>Why it matters:</strong> unlimited premium AI inside a moderately priced sub is economically unstable. Market separating into: ordinary features (sub), light AI (included), expensive AI (credits/usage), external agents (MCP).</p><p><strong>Report rec:</strong> ACT NOW — model light/medium/heavy usage classes; clear monthly allowance; explicit approval before expensive ops; avoid vague 'unlimited AI.'</p>", "type": "document", "parentId": "250f1cc9-166f-4d4f-88cc-df29b63ac518", "childrenIds": [], "isCollapsed": false, "prefix": "3.1.5", "metadata": {"createdAt": 1788552182282, "updatedAt": 1788552182282}}, "f819d744-f142-4826-83c9-7e834d6df54a": {"id": "f819d744-f142-4826-83c9-7e834d6df54a", "name": "⑥ Apple as both distribution channel and competitor", "content": "<p><strong>What changed:</strong> Apple's next platform gen gives third-party apps deeper access to Siri personal context, onscreen awareness, and cross-app actions via App Intents; unified model framework (on-device + server models, image input, custom skills); qualifying small developers get some Private Cloud Compute model access WITHOUT API charges. Siri positioned as a system-wide interface to find info and take actions in apps.</p><p><strong>Why it matters:</strong> we can't win as another isolated AI destination, but Siri could be a valuable entry point INTO IdeaM.</p><p><strong>Report rec:</strong> INVESTIGATE NOW; implement before iOS 27 maturity — audit our App Intents architecture; expose safe outline entities/actions to Siri without unrestricted editing authority.</p>", "type": "document", "parentId": "250f1cc9-166f-4d4f-88cc-df29b63ac518", "childrenIds": [], "isCollapsed": false, "prefix": "3.1.6", "metadata": {"createdAt": 1788552182282, "updatedAt": 1788552182282}}, "42090047-3c0b-4146-a3e8-7728fe17fc30": {"id": "42090047-3c0b-4146-a3e8-7728fe17fc30", "name": "Report’s three priorities + bottom line", "content": "<p><strong>Report's top 3:</strong> (1) Proposed Changes mode; (2) Natural-language dynamic outlines; (3) AI cost model (measure light/medium/heavy before pricing).</p><p><strong>Bottom line (report):</strong> the largest immediate opportunity is not adding another AI model — it's making AI actions structural, inspectable, and reversible inside the outline, where competitor UX is converging and our hierarchical model gives a natural advantage.</p>", "type": "document", "parentId": "250f1cc9-166f-4d4f-88cc-df29b63ac518", "childrenIds": [], "isCollapsed": false, "prefix": "3.1.7", "metadata": {"createdAt": 1788552182282, "updatedAt": 1788552182282}}, "1e8b808d-90ee-4b54-a1f1-1d4833292bd3": {"id": "1e8b808d-90ee-4b54-a1f1-1d4833292bd3", "name": "🟠 Our analysis (Claude)", "content": "<p><strong>Sharp point:</strong> the report's bottom line describes what we ALREADY claim to be. So the play is to ship the flagship version FIRST and loudly, not to chase.</p><p><strong>Per-item verdict → see Rolling Priorities:</strong></p>", "type": "chapter", "parentId": "250f1cc9-166f-4d4f-88cc-df29b63ac518", "childrenIds": ["5e258386-8019-40e4-a97f-ad8789419a40", "b04387bb-d595-4e6c-877d-14ec55661ce4", "5e5baf1f-38e1-4b45-bb2f-196e5a764c8d", "b188b3f0-f536-4618-8776-e4db95d12b2f", "69fc735b-f2ec-4e7b-8e23-c6be8943a45b", "fef92f0c-add8-42d1-9911-54592c2262e3"], "isCollapsed": false, "prefix": "3.1.8", "metadata": {"userEdited": true}}, "5e258386-8019-40e4-a97f-ad8789419a40": {"id": "5e258386-8019-40e4-a97f-ad8789419a40", "name": "Flagship = #2 Proposed Changes mode", "content": "<p>Strong agree; more natural for our hierarchy than for doc tools. Rolled up as <strong>P1</strong>.</p>", "type": "document", "parentId": "1e8b808d-90ee-4b54-a1f1-1d4833292bd3", "childrenIds": [], "isCollapsed": false, "prefix": "3.1.8.1", "metadata": {"createdAt": 1788552182282, "updatedAt": 1788552182282}}, "b04387bb-d595-4e6c-877d-14ec55661ce4": {"id": "b04387bb-d595-4e6c-877d-14ec55661ce4", "name": "#5 Cost model validates us", "content": "<p>We're ahead (no company key, BYOK, metered, guardrails). Sharpening: the new HEAVY media ops (Veo/Lyria) must sit on top of pre-op approval. Rolled up as <strong>P2</strong>.</p>", "type": "document", "parentId": "1e8b808d-90ee-4b54-a1f1-1d4833292bd3", "childrenIds": [], "isCollapsed": false, "prefix": "3.1.8.2", "metadata": {"createdAt": 1788552182282, "updatedAt": 1788552182282}}, "5e5baf1f-38e1-4b45-bb2f-196e5a764c8d": {"id": "5e5baf1f-38e1-4b45-bb2f-196e5a764c8d", "name": "#3 NL dynamic branches", "content": "<p>Agree; sequence after P1; align to the 1988 search-shaper spec. Rolled up as <strong>P3</strong>.</p>", "type": "document", "parentId": "1e8b808d-90ee-4b54-a1f1-1d4833292bd3", "childrenIds": [], "isCollapsed": false, "prefix": "3.1.8.3", "metadata": {"createdAt": 1788552182282, "updatedAt": 1788552182282}}, "b188b3f0-f536-4618-8776-e4db95d12b2f": {"id": "b188b3f0-f536-4618-8776-e4db95d12b2f", "name": "#4 Board view", "content": "<p>Good fit, not urgent — we already do mind-map/flowchart from a subtree. Rolled up as <strong>P4</strong>.</p>", "type": "document", "parentId": "1e8b808d-90ee-4b54-a1f1-1d4833292bd3", "childrenIds": [], "isCollapsed": false, "prefix": "3.1.8.4", "metadata": {"createdAt": 1788552182282, "updatedAt": 1788552182282}}, "69fc735b-f2ec-4e7b-8e23-c6be8943a45b": {"id": "69fc735b-f2ec-4e7b-8e23-c6be8943a45b", "name": "#6 Apple/Siri + PCC free-AI sleeper", "content": "<p>Strong distribution + a company-cost-free premium path worth chasing; needs native Swift work. Rolled up as <strong>P5</strong>.</p>", "type": "document", "parentId": "1e8b808d-90ee-4b54-a1f1-1d4833292bd3", "childrenIds": [], "isCollapsed": false, "prefix": "3.1.8.5", "metadata": {"createdAt": 1788552182282, "updatedAt": 1788552182282}}, "fef92f0c-add8-42d1-9911-54592c2262e3": {"id": "fef92f0c-add8-42d1-9911-54592c2262e3", "name": "#1 Voice-while-talking — the tension", "content": "<p>We deliberately pulled voice back to dictation-only; we won't reverse that. The useful half is P1. Rolled up as <strong>P6 (watch)</strong>.</p>", "type": "document", "parentId": "1e8b808d-90ee-4b54-a1f1-1d4833292bd3", "childrenIds": [], "isCollapsed": false, "prefix": "3.1.8.6", "metadata": {"createdAt": 1788552182282, "updatedAt": 1788552182282}}}}